            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Personal Life and Personality</strong><br>\nFeynman's vibrant personality and curiosity were as well-known as his scientific prowess. His candid autobiographical works provide insight into his life and the way he viewed the world.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Contributions to Physics Beyond QED</strong><br>\nFeynman's work extended beyond quantum electrodynamics to include areas such as quantum computing and nanotechnology. He was often ahead of his time, foreseeing future developments in physics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Posthumous Recognition</strong><br>\nFeynman died on February 15, 1988. His impact on physics is immeasurable, and his ability to communicate complex scientific principles in an accessible manner has made him a legend in the scientific community.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
